cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use impopk in academic work, please cite the paper bundled in paper/manuscript.pdf."
title: "impopk: local ancestry and IBD inference from pangenome-derived alignments"
abstract: >-
  impopk is a suite of Rust command-line tools that compute windowed
  pairwise identity from haplotype-resolved pangenome alignments and feed
  that signal to hidden Markov models for IBD detection, local ancestry
  inference, and kinship estimation, without requiring phased VCFs or a
  population-specific SNP panel.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarsicoFL/IMPOPk"
